#!/bin/sh
# Checks that each package declares the interpreters its shipped scripts need (no hardware needed).
# hanoip-qgd only ran because python3 happened to be installed on the phone; a fresh image would have
# no battery percentage, and a stuck percentage is how the battery once died.
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
bad=0
for apk in pmaports/device/*/*/APKBUILD; do
	d=$(dirname "$apk")
	deps=$(sed -n '/^depends="/,/"/p' "$apk")
	# With rust in makedepends, pmbootstrap's crossdirect installs every dependency in the x86_64 chroot,
	# and the aarch64-only ones (firmware, soc-qcom) do not exist there: the build stops before abuild.
	if grep -q '^makedepends=.*\brust\b' "$apk" && ! grep -q '^options=.*!pmb:crossdirect' "$apk"; then
		echo "FAIL: $apk builds rust but lacks options=!pmb:crossdirect" >&2
		bad=1
	fi
	for f in "$d"/*; do
		[ -f "$f" ] || continue
		case $(head -1 "$f") in
		'#!'*python3*) need=python3 ;;
		*) continue ;;
		esac
		echo "$deps" | grep -qw "$need" && continue
		echo "FAIL: $f needs $need, missing from depends in $apk" >&2
		bad=1
	done
done
# The other way round: python3 stays out of depends once no shipped script needs it (issue #22), so it cannot
# creep back in as a dependency nothing uses.
for apk in pmaports/device/*/*/APKBUILD; do
	d=$(dirname "$apk")
	sed -n '/^depends="/,/"/p' "$apk" | grep -qw python3 || continue
	used=0
	for f in "$d"/*; do
		[ -f "$f" ] || continue
		case $(head -1 "$f" 2>/dev/null) in '#!'*python3*) used=1 ;; esac
	done
	[ $used -eq 1 ] || { echo "FAIL: $apk depends on python3 but ships no python3 script" >&2; bad=1; }
done
# Duranium's mkosi looks for systemd-boot's EFI binary in the image and stops without it (2026-11-09: "a systemd-boot
# binary was not found at /usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi"). Nothing but the device package can pull it in, so the mainline
# kernel subpackage, the one the EFI path installs, depends on it.
apk=pmaports/device/testing/device-motorola-hanoip/APKBUILD
sed -n '/^kernel_mainline()/,/^}/p' "$apk" | grep -q 'depends=.*\bsystemd-boot\b' \
	|| { echo "FAIL: kernel_mainline() in $apk must depend on systemd-boot (Duranium's mkosi needs its EFI binary)" >&2; bad=1; }
[ $bad -eq 0 ] && echo "apkbuild depends: ok"
exit $bad
